Atlas3DSS fork modifications (Apache License 2.0)
-------------------------------------------------
Derived from satellitedown/inkling-2-mini-abliterated-ingine (commit 556acc7),
which incorporates code from satellitedown/fngine, cinference, and NInfer
(Apache License 2.0), and targets Thinking Machines' Inkling-2-Mini
(Apache License 2.0).

Modifications by Atlas3DSS:
- Multi-architecture CUDA port for Ampere (sm_86) and Ada (sm_89) alongside
  Blackwell (sm_120a), with CUDA 12.8 and CUDA 13.x compatibility and
  bit-identical Blackwell fast paths (48/48 kernels_bitlock PASS).
- Native sub-4-bit Elastic MoE weight formats (ATLAS2 2.50 b/w, ATLAS3 3.50 b/w)
  in decode and prefill kernels plus tools/quantize_elastic_ingine.py.
- 4-bit Q4_0 global KV cache (--kv-q4) for the 8 global full-attention visits
  (keeping all 40 SWA layers in BF16; 9 KiB/tok = 2.25 GiB at 262K context).
- Native EXL3 / Escha W2 MCG trellis + 128-point Hadamard MoE decode and prefill
  kernels (2-bit and 3-bit mixed-precision Map M2) and Q4_0 token embeddings:
  * EXL3 MCG trellis codebook (0xCBAC1FED, lop3 0x8fff8fff/0x3b603b60, hadd2),
    16x16 tail-biting ring bitstream, and tile_perm fragment layout derived from
    ExLlamaV3 (https://github.com/turboderp-org/exllamav3, MIT License,
    Copyright (c) turboderp and ExLlamaV3 contributors).
  * Escha W2 / Kintsugi-Inkling-2-Mini Map M2 expert quantization format and
    128-pt Sylvester Hadamard rotation layout compatible with EschaLabs
    escha-mlx and Kintsugi-Inkling-2-Mini (Apache License 2.0).
- Native OpenAI response_format (text, json_object, json_schema) and automatic
  tool-invocation token suppression when tools are omitted.
- Phase 3 target vendor backend slices (pure native C++20 AMD ROCm/HIP, Apple
  MLX/Metal, Intel SYCL/oneAPI HAL/Ops/policy primitives):
  * HIP device intrinsic compatibility mappings (v_perm_b32, sudot4/sdot4, SWAR
    vsub4, wave64 logical-32 half-wavefront ballot/sync, gfx11/gfx12 RDNA WMMA
    row mapping, EXL3 scalar prompt tile policy) and Metal parallel pread
    chunking patterns studied from Strata / Project Maya
    (https://github.com/Atlas3DSS/project-maya, MIT License).
  * HIP/SYCL CMake discovery patterns (oneAPI SYCL/icpx, Level Zero direct
    device allocation, oneMKL/oneDNN vendor guard) studied from ggml-hip and
    ggml-sycl in llama.cpp / atlas-engine (MIT License, Copyright (c) The ggml authors).
